  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Key Questions to Ask Before Converting a Garage into Living Space",
    "text": "Key Questions to Ask Before Converting a Garage into Living Space",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Converting an existing garage into usable living quarters is one of the most practical ways to add functional square footage, but it comes with distinct structural and regulatory hurdles. \n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide\nStart by asking if the garage structure can legally be classified as habitable space under local codes. Garages were often built under different construction standards than primary living quarters, which means foundations, slab conditions, and framing must be verified. Next, ask how moisture control and thermal insulation will be managed. Concrete slabs hold ground moisture, requiring vapor barriers and floor insulation, while exterior walls require proper thermal barriers to maintain comfortable temperatures. You also need to confirm whether dedicated heating and cooling circuits can connect to your current panel and whether external parking spots must be preserved to comply with zoning rules. Finally, clarify who oversees drawing approvals, permits, and inspections.\n\nHaving a knowledgeable general contractor manage framing, drywall, and finishes while coordinating licensed trade partners ensures a smooth transition. To review your garage conversion plans, call HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
